1
00:02:04,214 --> 00:02:08,344
No living creature was hurt during
the production of this show.

2
00:02:10,514 --> 00:02:17,574
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:03:03,195 --> 00:03:05,563
- My Bey.
- Ha?

4
00:03:05,563 --> 00:03:08,543
The woundeds are secured by Alps.

5
00:03:09,211 --> 00:03:14,611
Our Bamsı Bey's and our martyrs' bodies
are on their way to tent.

6
00:03:44,401 --> 00:03:49,841
Nothing. No traces of Nicola's dogs.
No traces of Togay's soldiers.

7
00:03:55,263 --> 00:03:56,813
Brother.

8
00:03:57,640 --> 00:04:00,000
You'll keep looking.

9
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,030
You'll search until you find them.

10
00:04:02,949 --> 00:04:05,779
If they are under the land...

11
00:04:06,234 --> 00:04:08,304
Pluck them off!

12
00:04:09,729 --> 00:04:12,429
If they are in hell...

13
00:04:12,590 --> 00:04:14,610
Take them out!

14
00:04:16,586 --> 00:04:20,916
If they are behind the mountains...

15
00:04:21,204 --> 00:04:24,414
Go through the mountains!

16
00:04:25,606 --> 00:04:28,126
They hurt my heart!

17
00:04:28,363 --> 00:04:34,703
They slaughtered my father's memorial
Bamsı Bey, they slaughtered my alps!

18
00:04:37,849 --> 00:04:41,719
They destroyed the head of my tent!

19
00:04:43,101 --> 00:04:50,351
They are not going to die easily.

20
00:04:56,196 --> 00:04:58,206
Let's go!

21
00:04:59,289 --> 00:05:05,689
Brother, depart at once!
Search everywhere to Inegol Castle.

22
00:05:06,763 --> 00:05:09,423
I'll go to Togay's place.

23
00:05:09,703 --> 00:05:11,633
As you command, my Bey.

24
00:05:11,744 --> 00:05:13,834
Let's go Alps!

25
00:05:23,208 --> 00:05:25,308
Go!

26
00:05:44,772 --> 00:05:48,692
Hurry up idiots!
Hurry up!

27
00:06:08,022 --> 00:06:10,412
Come here Osman.

28
00:06:12,631 --> 00:06:18,131
Osman will track us for taking revenge
for Bamsı Bey.

29
00:06:19,157 --> 00:06:24,307
When they come, you'll fall on them.

30
00:06:25,144 --> 00:06:30,814
You have to choke their souls.

31
00:06:31,073 --> 00:06:32,923
Don't worry Togay.

32
00:06:33,230 --> 00:06:38,510
The weakest point of a Gokboru like
Osman is his anger, Camuha.

33
00:06:40,927 --> 00:06:44,577
I baited him to my trap.

34
00:06:44,785 --> 00:06:49,505
He'll go mad and his
anger will lead him to death.

35
00:06:55,911 --> 00:06:57,751
Hurry up!

36
00:06:58,049 --> 00:07:00,769
It's time to get blood!

37
00:07:44,738 --> 00:07:46,438
My Bey.

38
00:07:49,256 --> 00:07:51,056
Cerkutay.

39
00:07:56,552 --> 00:07:58,632
They passed here.

40
00:08:01,605 --> 00:08:03,775
They're going to their place, my Bey.

41
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:08,290
My Bamsı Bey is watchin us...

42
00:08:08,862 --> 00:08:11,702
We'll track them down!

43
00:08:12,281 --> 00:08:15,471
We are the valiants who
follow him.

44
00:08:16,963 --> 00:08:18,573
Let's go.

45
00:08:18,969 --> 00:08:20,629
Let's go.

46
00:08:25,665 --> 00:08:27,965
Leave the horses here.

47
00:09:30,462 --> 00:09:32,352
Where are they my Bey?

48
00:09:33,685 --> 00:09:35,915
They must have realised we were coming.

49
00:09:54,817 --> 00:09:57,827
I am here Osman Bey!

50
00:10:05,820 --> 00:10:08,190
Osman Bey.

51
00:10:10,921 --> 00:10:14,421
Let's see what you are going to do now.

52
00:10:52,786 --> 00:10:55,296
Your path ends here, Osman.

53
00:10:55,774 --> 00:10:59,924
Your desire for revenge
turned you into a fool, Osman Bey!

54
00:11:00,003 --> 00:11:02,813
Otherwise you wouldn't fall in this trap.

55
00:11:02,977 --> 00:11:04,937
Get out of my way.

56
00:11:28,436 --> 00:11:32,806
Feelings of vengeance
turned me into a lion!

57
00:11:33,483 --> 00:11:36,423
Now you are between my paws!

58
00:14:21,410 --> 00:14:24,470
Protect me!
Protect me!

59
00:14:24,479 --> 00:14:26,399
Protect me!

60
00:15:04,806 --> 00:15:06,766
For Bamsı Bey!

61
00:15:41,715 --> 00:15:43,565
Attack!

62
00:16:04,689 --> 00:16:06,949
Where are you Togay?

63
00:16:07,227 --> 00:16:09,277
Where are you?

64
00:16:28,473 --> 00:16:30,803
As that Camuha dog run away...

65
00:16:34,057 --> 00:16:36,537
Togay must be somewhere else.

66
00:16:39,088 --> 00:16:41,158
We're returning to tent!

67
00:16:43,739 --> 00:16:46,829
We'll complete our last mission
for Bamsı Bey.

68
00:16:47,224 --> 00:16:51,714
Later, we'll find those heathens!

69
00:16:53,187 --> 00:16:55,367
Let's go!

70
00:17:08,309 --> 00:17:09,879
Bamsı..

71
00:17:10,818 --> 00:17:14,808
Crazy Bamsı has died,
is that true?

72
00:17:18,558 --> 00:17:20,165
He's dead.

73
00:17:20,886 --> 00:17:24,926
He roared an died.

74
00:17:33,092 --> 00:17:39,222
Abdurrahman Ghazi, Savcı Bey
and finally Bamsı.

75
00:17:40,221 --> 00:17:44,331
Ertugrul Ghazi's era has ended
with Bamsı.

76
00:17:44,366 --> 00:17:47,406
Now it's time for his breed.

77
00:17:47,785 --> 00:17:52,095
Osman will go after you, you know that.

78
00:17:53,319 --> 00:17:57,675
This is what we want.
He'll disobey Geyhatu...

79
00:17:57,675 --> 00:18:00,175
because of his anger...

80
00:18:00,246 --> 00:18:02,651
and he'll ruin himself and
others like Umur Bey...

81
00:18:02,651 --> 00:18:05,261
Disobeying Geyhatu means death.

82
00:18:07,345 --> 00:18:11,795
You have to be loyal to Geyhatu, and
create an army with your soldiers.

83
00:18:11,930 --> 00:18:15,510
We are going to hit Osman together.

84
00:18:19,751 --> 00:18:25,731
Are you sweating, Nicola?

85
00:18:29,102 --> 00:18:33,822
You were the one who killed
Yason's soldiers, Togay.

86
00:18:35,085 --> 00:18:39,825
It won't be easy to take
soldiers from Governors.

87
00:18:41,817 --> 00:18:44,257
I have to think about it.

88
00:18:45,772 --> 00:18:49,982
If you want Geyhatu's friendship,
do not think.

89
00:18:50,398 --> 00:18:53,178
Just fight.
Find soldiers.

90
00:18:53,278 --> 00:18:55,108
Create an army.

91
00:18:55,213 --> 00:19:00,093
Otherwise, our alliance will
turn into hostility.

92
00:19:03,183 --> 00:19:06,443
I give you time until
tomorrow sunset.

93
00:19:06,802 --> 00:19:11,442
I suggest you not to
make me angry.

94
00:19:31,994 --> 00:19:35,504
Army aside, I won't even give you
a soldier!

95
00:19:36,334 --> 00:19:38,754
What about Vali Yargucu?

96
00:19:40,199 --> 00:19:43,761
I'll sound governors out.

97
00:19:43,761 --> 00:19:46,031
We both now they'll reject, Nicola!

98
00:19:46,071 --> 00:19:50,691
Of course Helen!
This will be our excuse!

99
00:20:19,356 --> 00:20:22,086
How did Osman get out of there?

100
00:20:22,402 --> 00:20:25,982
- I don't know how it happened.
- Shut up!

101
00:20:28,523 --> 00:20:30,023
Gokboru...

102
00:20:31,810 --> 00:20:36,410
I'll leave you to kill Nicola's soldiers!

103
00:20:37,292 --> 00:20:41,742
Nicola is going to find out you
disobeyed Vali Yargucu.

104
00:20:42,527 --> 00:20:46,817
I'll use him until he finds out.

105
00:20:53,072 --> 00:20:57,482
"We had placed collars around their necks, right up
to their chins so that their heads are forced up

106
00:20:57,510 --> 00:21:02,215
We set barriers before and behind them,
blocking their vision: they cannot see.

107
00:21:02,215 --> 00:21:05,528
It is all the same to them whether...

108
00:21:05,528 --> 00:21:08,453
you warn them or not:
they will not believe.

109
00:21:08,453 --> 00:21:14,453
You can warn only those who will follow the
Quran and hold the Merciful One in awe,

110
00:21:14,453 --> 00:21:20,562
though they cannot see Him: give such people
the glad news of forgiveness and a noble reward.

111
00:21:20,562 --> 00:21:23,972
We shall certainly bring the dead back to life,
and We record what they send ahead of them

112
00:21:23,972 --> 00:21:27,423
as well as what they leave behind:

113
00:21:27,423 --> 00:21:30,917
We keep an account of everything in a clear record.

114
00:21:30,943 --> 00:21:36,788
Give them the example of the people
to whose town messengers came.

115
00:21:36,893 --> 00:21:40,667
We sent two messengers
but they rejected both.

116
00:21:40,667 --> 00:21:44,320
Then We reinforced them with a third.

117
00:21:44,320 --> 00:21:47,510
They said, ‘Truly,
we are messengers to you,’

118
00:21:47,516 --> 00:21:51,535
but they answered, ‘You are only
men like ourselves.

119
00:21:51,535 --> 00:21:58,085
The Lord of Mercy has sent nothing;
you are just lying.'

120
00:21:58,355 --> 00:22:00,455
Surah Yasin [9-16]

121
00:22:30,172 --> 00:22:35,242
When a ghazi dies,
when a valiant is martyred...

122
00:22:36,398 --> 00:22:43,108
We need to remember them with
their battles they had.

123
00:22:44,605 --> 00:22:49,715
I remember Bamsı Bey as a valiant...

124
00:22:50,406 --> 00:22:56,036
whose heart beats for fighting
for Allah, for his religion.

125
00:22:59,761 --> 00:23:03,691
- May Allah bless him.
- Amin.

126
00:23:04,759 --> 00:23:06,429
Amin.

127
00:23:12,209 --> 00:23:16,829
When I was a kid, ever time my father
Ertugrul Ghazi...

128
00:23:17,450 --> 00:23:21,440
- May Allah bless him
- Amin.

129
00:23:21,755 --> 00:23:26,625
goes to war, I was thinking...

130
00:23:27,288 --> 00:23:30,128
if Bamsı Bey was with him or not.

131
00:23:32,930 --> 00:23:37,070
His existence gave me confidince.

132
00:23:38,576 --> 00:23:42,046
I'd say "good, very good...

133
00:23:42,600 --> 00:23:46,630
Bamsı Bey with double sword
is with my father."

134
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:51,180
Good times old times.

135
00:23:54,759 --> 00:23:57,239
Then we grew up.

136
00:24:01,706 --> 00:24:06,406
He respected us because we
were sons of a Bey...

137
00:24:06,765 --> 00:24:09,695
but he still educated us.

138
00:24:10,621 --> 00:24:15,481
- May Allah bless him.
- Amin.

139
00:24:18,272 --> 00:24:21,302
I am glad to...

140
00:24:23,288 --> 00:24:26,848
have a friendship with Bamsı Bey.

141
00:24:29,421 --> 00:24:32,061
He was massive like a lion.

142
00:24:34,076 --> 00:24:36,606
But his heart was like a bird.

143
00:24:36,976 --> 00:24:40,256
I saw him tearing up many times.

144
00:24:41,726 --> 00:24:46,076
He was worried about Kayı.
He got happy for Kayı.

145
00:24:51,608 --> 00:24:54,230
People thought he had
no pain inside.

146
00:24:54,230 --> 00:24:59,450
However, his sorrow was great
for his martyred son.

147
00:25:03,711 --> 00:25:08,211
Everybody knew his name, even our tribe.

148
00:25:09,591 --> 00:25:16,560
As we heard about Ertugrul Ghazi's wars,
people would say "There is this Bamsı...

149
00:25:17,183 --> 00:25:22,273
who is the man, who is the archer,
who is the warrior."

150
00:25:23,798 --> 00:25:27,498
Everybody knew his name.

151
00:25:28,182 --> 00:25:32,876
Then we came here, and
saw him face to face.

152
00:25:32,876 --> 00:25:36,416
We figured he was even underrated.

153
00:25:37,199 --> 00:25:42,969
- May he rest in heaven.
- Amin.

154
00:25:45,374 --> 00:25:47,284
Ertugrul Ghazi...

155
00:25:48,917 --> 00:25:50,927
Savcı Bey...

156
00:25:52,731 --> 00:25:55,351
Abdurrahman Ghazi...

157
00:25:56,830 --> 00:25:59,520
And now...

158
00:26:01,224 --> 00:26:03,324
Bamsı Bey.

159
00:26:05,490 --> 00:26:08,090
Massive valiants...

160
00:26:09,532 --> 00:26:12,852
Massive valiants are under the soil.

161
00:26:19,865 --> 00:26:24,245
If we don't raise new valiants
like them...

162
00:26:25,494 --> 00:26:28,134
to take their place...

163
00:26:28,959 --> 00:26:31,599
we'll have hard times.

164
00:26:37,579 --> 00:26:39,979
We'll stand up.

165
00:26:41,721 --> 00:26:46,131
We'll eternize their willing to fight.

166
00:26:49,077 --> 00:26:56,187
We'll struggle for them, we'll
work for their memorial.

167
00:26:58,333 --> 00:27:01,063
Inshallah (if Allah permits.)

168
00:27:01,194 --> 00:27:03,634
Eyvallah (Thank you) Osman Bey.

169
00:27:07,883 --> 00:27:10,738
We shall not keep you any longer,
Osman Bey.

170
00:27:10,738 --> 00:27:12,816
Bismillah.
(In the name of Allah).

171
00:27:12,816 --> 00:27:15,656
Not at all, my Sheik.

172
00:27:16,398 --> 00:27:18,568
You honored me.

173
00:27:21,025 --> 00:27:22,635
My Sheik.

174
00:27:30,242 --> 00:27:33,822
Osman Bey, I shall leave too.

175
00:27:34,692 --> 00:27:37,682
Umur Bey, you can wait.

176
00:27:38,051 --> 00:27:41,781
Our path is same now.

177
00:27:44,840 --> 00:27:50,000
Let's sit down and talk
about our upcoming moves.

178
00:27:54,199 --> 00:27:57,559
Eyvallah Osman Bey,
Thank you.

179
00:27:57,905 --> 00:27:59,845
Here.

180
00:28:26,543 --> 00:28:29,773
I want to be a martyr too.

181
00:28:31,648 --> 00:28:35,668
My Bey, why do you want it?

182
00:28:42,963 --> 00:28:45,373
I'll see my prophet.

183
00:28:47,349 --> 00:28:51,127
This is how things go, Cerkutay.

184
00:28:51,127 --> 00:28:54,957
Some leave, some stay.

185
00:28:56,234 --> 00:28:57,884
Cerkutay.

186
00:28:58,936 --> 00:29:00,826
Take them Cerkutay.

187
00:29:00,956 --> 00:29:04,366
Those are yours now.

188
00:29:07,485 --> 00:29:11,105
FATHER!

189
00:29:43,384 --> 00:29:46,054
And now my father deceased, Aygül.

190
00:30:08,634 --> 00:30:12,164
You were right, Dündar Bey.

191
00:30:12,164 --> 00:30:17,684
I tried to kill him many times.
We swung our blades at each other.

192
00:30:19,464 --> 00:30:23,464
But the day I came to the tribe.

193
00:30:24,390 --> 00:30:28,090
He took me into his tribe.

194
00:30:32,131 --> 00:30:35,741
So, he trusted you.

195
00:30:37,345 --> 00:30:39,945
So did...

196
00:30:40,129 --> 00:30:43,139
So did I!

197
00:30:45,635 --> 00:30:48,765
I took shelter in him.

198
00:30:51,639 --> 00:30:54,899
I took his support.

199
00:30:59,737 --> 00:31:03,157
Now I'm all alone.

200
00:31:21,807 --> 00:31:25,807
You have your brothers.

201
00:31:25,807 --> 00:31:29,807
You, Boran, and Göktuğ.
Aren't you three hawks?

202
00:31:36,242 --> 00:31:38,552
True.

203
00:31:40,818 --> 00:31:44,818
And also, you have me.

204
00:32:03,852 --> 00:32:07,292
And Ahmet too!

205
00:32:18,362 --> 00:32:20,512
Look.

206
00:32:21,983 --> 00:32:25,983
Bamsı Bey left a son like him
behind him.

207
00:32:26,156 --> 00:32:31,776
He told you that you'll be
Osman Bey's Bamsı now.

208
00:32:32,465 --> 00:32:37,495
He did.
He did.

209
00:32:42,468 --> 00:32:45,988
But it's not easy to be Bamsı Bey.

210
00:32:46,810 --> 00:32:51,360
Why are you saying that Cerkutay?
You have a good heart like him.

211
00:32:52,506 --> 00:32:55,976
You are strong like him.

212
00:33:00,334 --> 00:33:04,084
You are impatient like him.

213
00:33:04,084 --> 00:33:08,084
And Bamsı Bey too would make everyone
laugh back then.

214
00:33:42,575 --> 00:33:45,305
Son...

215
00:34:09,666 --> 00:34:15,116
So, what happened that Togay
broke the agreement?

216
00:34:15,327 --> 00:34:22,067
If he had such intentions before,
he wouldn't let me alive.

217
00:34:22,067 --> 00:34:27,657
What happened has happened.
We unsheathed our weapons.

218
00:34:29,188 --> 00:34:34,818
They won't be sheathed before getting
wet by the blood of that heathen.

219
00:34:41,315 --> 00:34:45,218
I sent news to our sultan.

220
00:34:45,218 --> 00:34:50,298
He should know that we didn't break
the agreement but he did.

221
00:34:50,770 --> 00:34:54,840
I wanted him to act accordingly.

222
00:34:57,863 --> 00:35:05,193
In this caravan raid, not only Togay's
warriors...

223
00:35:06,331 --> 00:35:11,271
but also Nikola's soldiers too were there.
-It was Nikola who sold me to Togay.

224
00:35:11,365 --> 00:35:16,215
He must've done it to gain Togay's
friendship.

225
00:35:17,281 --> 00:35:21,281
The grudge they hold against us
brought them together.

226
00:35:21,281 --> 00:35:25,831
But we'll separate them again.

227
00:35:27,155 --> 00:35:32,305
We'll break their dirty alliance...

228
00:35:32,305 --> 00:35:35,615
and crush them one by one.

229
00:35:35,615 --> 00:35:39,615
But firstly, Togay.

230
00:35:39,945 --> 00:35:43,945
I'll take care of him first.

231
00:35:54,395 --> 00:35:58,395
He was a duel-wielder.

232
00:35:58,395 --> 00:36:02,395
We would draw our swords when
he said: ''Come on, children!''

233
00:36:14,122 --> 00:36:18,122
It's enough that you hurt
yourself, Cerkutay.

234
00:36:18,122 --> 00:36:22,742
He wasn't just your father.
Bamsı Bey was a father to us all.

235
00:36:22,742 --> 00:36:26,382
He was the father of all ghazis.

236
00:36:27,470 --> 00:36:31,700
We are all in pain.
Ahmet Alp.

237
00:36:32,890 --> 00:36:35,650
Give me the swords.

238
00:36:41,780 --> 00:36:45,780
Wait! What are you doing?

239
00:36:47,267 --> 00:36:51,697
Cerkutay, it's Osman Bey's order.

240
00:36:52,376 --> 00:36:57,556
These weapons are the honor and history
of the last ghazi from our old lands.

241
00:36:57,675 --> 00:37:01,675
For this reason, these weapons
are very important.

242
00:37:01,675 --> 00:37:07,675
They'll go to where they are belong,
Osman Bey's tent.

243
00:37:10,916 --> 00:37:15,606
-Cerkutay! Cerkutay!
-Alright, alright. Wait.

244
00:37:16,018 --> 00:37:20,018
Let Cerkutay spend some time
and say farewell.

245
00:37:21,416 --> 00:37:24,656
But this isn't fair!

246
00:37:24,733 --> 00:37:28,743
Come on, there is no time.
They are going to the tent.

247
00:37:28,743 --> 00:37:30,993
What are you saying?

248
00:37:31,628 --> 00:37:36,398
-Cerkutay!
-I would die before giving them!

249
00:37:37,089 --> 00:37:41,959
Cerkutay, are you disobeying
Osman Bey's orders, brother?

250
00:37:42,087 --> 00:37:46,727
-Come on.
-Bamsı Bey gave them to me. You know it.

251
00:37:46,774 --> 00:37:51,584
He gave them to me. If Osman Bey ordered
it, alright, but...

252
00:37:51,967 --> 00:37:55,967
Cerkutay! Say farewell.

253
00:37:56,644 --> 00:38:00,644
This is Osman Bey's order.

254
00:38:03,362 --> 00:38:07,362
Come on, brother.
Come on.

255
00:38:24,144 --> 00:38:28,144
O' good Bamsı Bey!

256
00:38:33,863 --> 00:38:39,625
We wanted to herald these two weapons...

257
00:38:39,625 --> 00:38:45,425
to the new and real owner of them
after Bamsı Bey.

258
00:38:45,425 --> 00:38:49,425
We wanted our brother to feel proud.

259
00:39:01,311 --> 00:39:05,121
With the name of Allah.

260
00:39:20,845 --> 00:39:24,015
My brother.

261
00:39:36,804 --> 00:39:42,914
So, you played with Cerkutay? Bamsı Bey
would laugh a lot if he was here.

262
00:39:42,914 --> 00:39:49,134
-You played with me, huh?
-Yes. Come.

263
00:40:51,659 --> 00:40:57,459
We will avenge him...
We'll make Togay puke blood!

264
00:40:59,852 --> 00:41:03,852
We swear! We swear!
We swear!

265
00:41:06,519 --> 00:41:11,289
But you will pay for this joke.

266
00:41:13,180 --> 00:41:18,000
With these weapons, I will avenge
Bamsı Bey first.

267
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:23,060
Then, I will avenge for
deceiving Cerkutay like this.

268
00:41:23,060 --> 00:41:27,470
What will you do to them, you crazy man?

269
00:41:30,332 --> 00:41:35,852
It's my responsibility to take
a worthy revenge.

270
00:41:38,607 --> 00:41:45,017
What will I do to you?
What will I do to you?

271
00:42:10,272 --> 00:42:14,012
With the name of Allah.

272
00:42:22,461 --> 00:42:27,201
My daughter.
My dear daughter.

273
00:42:27,961 --> 00:42:30,591
My Malhun.

274
00:42:30,591 --> 00:42:35,181
Thank Allah that I've seen
your happiness.

275
00:42:37,361 --> 00:42:41,651
And you married a valiant bey.

276
00:42:42,148 --> 00:42:46,148
You came to a noble and
famous tribe.

277
00:42:48,536 --> 00:42:53,256
Now, tell me.
Is everything as you wanted?

278
00:43:00,057 --> 00:43:03,901
I knew that I was coming to a
tribe with a Khatun.

279
00:43:03,901 --> 00:43:07,681
So, I didn't expect everything to be
as I wanted.

280
00:43:12,297 --> 00:43:14,937
Look, daughter...

281
00:43:15,775 --> 00:43:20,155
there are two kinds
of people in this world.

282
00:43:20,155 --> 00:43:24,155
Good and bad people.

283
00:43:24,155 --> 00:43:30,565
The hostility, hatred, and anger
of the bad never ends.

284
00:43:31,476 --> 00:43:37,056
Because the source is the
darkness in their hearts.

285
00:43:38,576 --> 00:43:45,176
But there are no hatred or grudge
in the hearts of the good.

286
00:43:45,303 --> 00:43:48,813
Their hostility is temporal.

287
00:43:48,813 --> 00:43:52,813
After all, their hearts
are clean.

288
00:43:52,813 --> 00:43:56,343
Clean hearts can't keep hostility
for long.

289
00:44:00,922 --> 00:44:03,552
My pretty daughter.

290
00:44:04,842 --> 00:44:09,692
I vouch for you. I know that
your heart is clean.

291
00:44:11,712 --> 00:44:15,712
And about Bala Hatun.

292
00:44:16,072 --> 00:44:21,942
Even a wood can't leave devious
from Edebali's lodge.

293
00:44:25,971 --> 00:44:31,201
But we were devious.

294
00:44:33,424 --> 00:44:38,724
We left the word we gave him.
And we paid the price.

295
00:44:39,584 --> 00:44:42,754
Not at all, father.

296
00:44:43,456 --> 00:44:47,456
It is, it is. We were blind.

297
00:44:48,244 --> 00:44:52,244
Edebali is the light of the Turks.

298
00:44:53,430 --> 00:44:57,430
We were without the light and blinded.

299
00:45:04,662 --> 00:45:09,292
So, what I'm saying is...

300
00:45:09,908 --> 00:45:13,908
be patient. Be patient.

301
00:45:21,040 --> 00:45:26,170
You raised me, father.
And you still do.

302
00:45:32,118 --> 00:45:36,808
May Allah protect you.

303
00:46:08,217 --> 00:46:11,477
May I enter?

304
00:46:15,951 --> 00:46:18,441
Come.

305
00:46:23,592 --> 00:46:28,552
-I've talked to Zoe. She'll come tomorrow.
-Bring her to me directly.

306
00:47:02,084 --> 00:47:07,604
Osman, I know...
I know...

307
00:47:07,975 --> 00:47:13,055
You will avenge me.

308
00:47:15,660 --> 00:47:20,960
But, firstly...
Firstly...

309
00:47:21,163 --> 00:47:24,403
Think for my children.

310
00:47:34,166 --> 00:47:37,536
May I enter, my bey?

311
00:47:38,927 --> 00:47:41,367
Come.

312
00:48:05,596 --> 00:48:13,086
Thank Allah, Osman. He lives as
he wanted and died as he lived.

313
00:48:15,215 --> 00:48:19,635
-We witnessed it.
-We have, Bala.

314
00:48:21,359 --> 00:48:24,249
We witnessed it.

315
00:48:24,617 --> 00:48:29,297
And we'll avenge him.
Soon, inshlalah.

316
00:48:29,297 --> 00:48:31,347
Soon.

317
00:48:32,071 --> 00:48:36,071
May Allah keep your sword sharp, Osman.

318
00:48:37,309 --> 00:48:41,809
May Allah give you strenght.

319
00:48:48,708 --> 00:48:54,248
Bala, you are supporting me.

320
00:48:55,129 --> 00:48:57,639
You stand beside me.

321
00:48:59,334 --> 00:49:03,334
Until death knocks on my door, Osman.

322
00:49:03,815 --> 00:49:09,195
You are the pole of my tent.

323
00:49:38,135 --> 00:49:44,265
Alps! If the enemy thinks twice,
you'll think treble.

324
00:49:45,213 --> 00:49:50,733
You will think of the places that even
the devil can't!

325
00:49:51,477 --> 00:49:56,677
Arms, armpit, belt...

326
00:49:57,225 --> 00:50:02,145
legs, boots, every place!

327
00:50:05,257 --> 00:50:07,747
Caps!

328
00:50:10,677 --> 00:50:14,677
Back! Every place!

329
00:50:15,784 --> 00:50:19,784
Do you understand? Come on!

330
00:50:38,565 --> 00:50:41,665
Just like that.

331
00:50:54,756 --> 00:50:56,776
Zoe?

332
00:50:59,123 --> 00:51:02,093
Tell me, why are you here?

333
00:51:02,093 --> 00:51:07,123
First, you invited me to the tribe.
Now, Malhun Hatun did.

334
00:51:08,096 --> 00:51:12,096
Malhun Hatun? Why?

335
00:51:12,096 --> 00:51:16,096
I'll find out if you allow me.

336
00:51:19,105 --> 00:51:21,125
Alps!

337
00:51:29,698 --> 00:51:33,168
Come on alps, go on!

338
00:52:08,016 --> 00:52:12,386
My bey, he wants to speak.

339
00:52:17,528 --> 00:52:22,058
-Tell me.
-Firstly, my condolences, Osman Bey.

340
00:52:25,600 --> 00:52:28,360
May Allah bless you.

341
00:52:29,796 --> 00:52:32,626
Tell me.

342
00:52:32,910 --> 00:52:35,710
I've changed my mind.

343
00:52:37,841 --> 00:52:41,841
If you still want it, I want to
sell me property.

344
00:52:43,773 --> 00:52:47,773
What made you change your decision?

345
00:52:53,607 --> 00:52:57,097
I thought that this would be the best.

346
00:53:03,815 --> 00:53:09,305
Our wound is still fresh.
Let us talk this later.

347
00:53:11,290 --> 00:53:15,290
-Then allow me.
-Of course.

348
00:53:17,492 --> 00:53:20,882
-Boran.
-Yes, my bey.

349
00:53:25,172 --> 00:53:29,172
We'll talk about this later.

350
00:53:30,201 --> 00:53:33,091
-As you order, my bey.
-Go.

351
00:53:38,318 --> 00:53:41,898
-My bey.
-Tell me.

352
00:53:42,866 --> 00:53:46,336
It's from Konya Palace, my bey.

353
00:53:59,344 --> 00:54:03,344
Call my brother and Davud Bey
to my tent.

354
00:54:07,373 --> 00:54:12,683
I'll talk to Osman Bey. If it's good
with you, I want you to be with us.

355
00:54:13,117 --> 00:54:17,497
You'll be a company for Yaren
and see us as your family.

356
00:54:17,497 --> 00:54:22,897
Thank you, Malhun Hatun.
I was at a fruit garden for years.

357
00:54:23,393 --> 00:54:26,753
I've never had a family.

358
00:54:28,183 --> 00:54:31,903
No one treated me like you did before.
I don't know what to say.

359
00:54:31,903 --> 00:54:37,923
You don't need to say a thing. They'll
prepare a tent for you. Your new home.

360
00:54:39,760 --> 00:54:43,760
May it be good, then, Zoe.

361
00:54:43,760 --> 00:54:47,760
Thank you, Malhun Hatun.
You won't regret it.

362
00:54:59,524 --> 00:55:03,764
You held the hand of a lonely woman.
You made her happy.

363
00:55:03,764 --> 00:55:07,764
May Allah bless you. But, you are
Malhun Hatun.

364
00:55:08,337 --> 00:55:13,537
You never act without a plan.
Tell me, what's on your mind?

365
00:55:13,756 --> 00:55:19,356
I've done what I should, Alaca.
We shouldn't be alone.

366
00:55:20,950 --> 00:55:25,990
She knows the area, especially
Söğüt. She'll accompany us well.

367
00:55:38,923 --> 00:55:41,163
Zoe!

368
00:55:47,692 --> 00:55:52,412
What did you talk about with Malhun Hatun?
-Why are you curious?

369
00:55:52,471 --> 00:55:56,471
Wouldn't I be curious?
And I...

370
00:55:58,233 --> 00:56:03,733
-What about you?
-I'm curious, don't you get it?

371
00:56:04,268 --> 00:56:07,468
And I say why.

372
00:56:10,130 --> 00:56:14,130
I think about you.
Don't you understand?

373
00:56:14,313 --> 00:56:18,313
Do you think about everyone who
visits the tribe?

374
00:56:23,328 --> 00:56:26,698
I think about you.

375
00:56:32,335 --> 00:56:34,525
Zoe!

376
00:56:40,436 --> 00:56:43,626
Won't you say a thing?

377
00:56:44,629 --> 00:56:47,989
Malhun Hatun took me under
her service.

378
00:56:50,844 --> 00:56:54,844
Malhun Hatun? How so?

379
00:56:54,844 --> 00:57:00,204
Alaca. She praised me a lot.
She said that I can do anything.

380
00:57:00,431 --> 00:57:04,431
She can watch over the chickens
and ducks here.

381
00:57:04,431 --> 00:57:07,161
She'll have a place to call home and
have a good life, she told her.

382
00:57:07,273 --> 00:57:11,593
-So?
-So, I'm a tribeswoman now.

383
00:57:11,967 --> 00:57:15,147
I'll live in Kayı Tribe now.

384
00:57:27,804 --> 00:57:32,894
-Why are you smiling?
-I haven't heard such good news lately.

385
00:57:33,094 --> 00:57:37,974
-So, you are happy?
-Happy? I want to fly!

386
00:57:49,064 --> 00:57:53,064
Come, let's get your things.
Then, I'll show you around.

387
00:58:08,326 --> 00:58:13,946
Sultan Mesut says that Togay rebelled
against the Mongol governor.

388
00:58:16,421 --> 00:58:20,801
Now, Togay is a rebel.

389
00:58:21,185 --> 00:58:25,185
And we aren't facing the Ilkhaganete!

390
00:58:25,600 --> 00:58:30,690
When we go after him, no one will
stand behind him.

391
00:58:30,826 --> 00:58:34,826
And if we break his alliance
with Nikola...

392
00:58:35,665 --> 00:58:38,475
Sooner or later...

393
00:58:39,424 --> 00:58:44,334
with or without Nikola,
he'll die by my hands.

394
00:58:44,956 --> 00:58:48,956
-May I enter, my bey?
-Come in!

395
00:58:54,243 --> 00:58:58,723
-My bey, the lord of Bilecik is here.
-Take him in.

396
00:59:13,353 --> 00:59:15,723
Come.

397
00:59:21,678 --> 00:59:26,048
-My condolences, Osman Bey.
-Thank you. Thank you.

398
00:59:26,048 --> 00:59:30,798
I want to express my sincere empathy
for Bamsı Bey's deah.

399
00:59:31,088 --> 00:59:33,578
Thank you.

400
00:59:36,264 --> 00:59:39,904
-I have important news, Osman Bey.
-Tell me.

401
00:59:39,904 --> 00:59:46,564
Lately, Mongols visit İnegöl Castle
frequently.

402
00:59:48,114 --> 00:59:54,854
Not only you, my friend, but also
the emperor won't like this.

403
00:59:56,504 --> 00:59:59,884
I have an ear in the castle.

404
00:59:59,884 --> 01:00:05,284
As I heard, Togay wanted Nikola
to gather men to attack you.

405
01:00:09,785 --> 01:00:13,015
He'll go to the lords.

406
01:00:13,015 --> 01:00:17,045
Even though it will be difficult, they'll
build a big army.

407
01:00:17,045 --> 01:00:20,665
You must know what they want
to do with it.

408
01:00:20,697 --> 01:00:24,727
We know what they'll want to do.

409
01:00:26,897 --> 01:00:32,647
The important thing is what we will do.

410
01:00:39,924 --> 01:00:43,924
Thank Allah we did as Bamsı Bey
wanted.

411
01:00:44,206 --> 01:00:48,536
With the money he left, many poor
people filled their stomachs.

412
01:00:48,536 --> 01:00:52,536
-Thank Allah. May Allah protect our tribe.
-Amin.

413
01:01:02,788 --> 01:01:07,528
-Good day, ladies.
-Thank you, Malhun Hatun.

414
01:01:12,754 --> 01:01:19,374
-Who is our guest?
-Her name is Zoe. She'll be my helper.

415
01:01:20,094 --> 01:01:24,634
There were many women to help
Osman Bey's wife in the tribe.

416
01:01:38,550 --> 01:01:43,090
What does that indicate, Bala Hatun.
I want to know.

417
01:01:43,090 --> 01:01:47,090
If my word meant something,
I would ask earlier, Malhun Hatun.

418
01:01:53,599 --> 01:01:58,309
She is honest. She is capable.

419
01:01:58,437 --> 01:02:02,437
She is diligent and she has
no family.

420
01:02:02,437 --> 01:02:07,397
-And I opened my arms.
-Mashallah. Good thinking.

421
01:02:09,330 --> 01:02:12,960
Bala Hatun!

422
01:02:24,382 --> 01:02:29,082
I show you respect and
I expect respect.

423
01:02:30,815 --> 01:02:36,295
I remind you that no one is in a position
to question or order the other.

424
01:02:36,742 --> 01:02:41,352
I didn't question nor order.
I just reminded.

425
01:02:41,352 --> 01:02:45,352
If you'll do as you want, don't let
me stop you.

426
01:02:53,758 --> 01:02:57,318
I've heard it by an accident.

427
01:02:58,297 --> 01:03:02,297
Did Malhun Hatun do something
to bother you?

428
01:03:03,477 --> 01:03:08,647
New people come to the tribe every day.
Isn't it my right to know who they are?

429
01:03:17,183 --> 01:03:20,753
It's been days only...

430
01:03:20,753 --> 01:03:23,533
and she is forming her own order.

431
01:03:23,533 --> 01:03:28,753
Both Bala and Malhun Hatun doesn't
seem to step back.

432
01:03:28,942 --> 01:03:34,152
It's up to you, to their friends,
to hold them back.

433
01:03:35,608 --> 01:03:40,638
Osman Bey has a lot to do.
He shouldn't hear this.

434
01:04:03,716 --> 01:04:08,816
The time I've given you is over, Nikola
Will you fight like a soldier?

435
01:04:08,816 --> 01:04:12,816
Or will you let me bury you under
this stone tent with my warriors...

436
01:04:12,816 --> 01:04:17,166
by staying here like a woman?
-My army is ready!

437
01:04:22,128 --> 01:04:25,688
You can't do this, sir.

438
01:04:29,970 --> 01:04:32,590
Yaso...

439
01:04:33,578 --> 01:04:37,578
will bring 200 more soldiers from
the other lords...

440
01:04:37,578 --> 01:04:41,578
and we'll strike the last blow
on Osman together.

441
01:04:42,027 --> 01:04:46,027
You look very fiery to spill blood,
Nikola...

442
01:04:46,027 --> 01:04:50,027
you are growling here like a jackal
that smelled blood...

443
01:04:50,027 --> 01:04:55,577
but you too know that blood makes a jackal
crazy but it's not enough to beat its fear!

444
01:04:55,577 --> 01:04:58,777
I wanted to spill the blood of the Turks
for years, Togay!

445
01:04:58,777 --> 01:05:04,087
-Now, you roar like a tiger!
-I'm neither a jackal nor a tiger!

446
01:05:04,087 --> 01:05:10,717
I'm a soldier, Togay! A good soldier
who knows the price of losing you.

447
01:05:25,362 --> 01:05:27,782
The door!

448
01:05:31,398 --> 01:05:36,268
Why? Why did you do this, sir?

449
01:05:37,494 --> 01:05:42,064
Live the moment.
Don't trust tomorrow at all.

450
01:05:45,772 --> 01:05:48,972
I'm a soldier!

451
01:06:24,002 --> 01:06:29,562
-Welcome, my bey.
-Thank you. Thank you.

452
01:06:31,160 --> 01:06:36,950
In many battles, you stood by me
with this sword.

453
01:06:38,634 --> 01:06:42,694
I'm concerned that I won't
be with you anymore.

454
01:06:42,694 --> 01:06:45,924
You are a Khatun of this
tribe now.

455
01:06:49,916 --> 01:06:53,916
You can't put yourself at risk.

456
01:06:54,796 --> 01:06:59,326
I want to be with my alps and
take revenge from Togay.

457
01:07:05,657 --> 01:07:10,623
Tomorrow, we'll take revenge on them...

458
01:07:10,623 --> 01:07:16,223
at Kızılbey Ormanı, for every soldier
and woman of the tribe.

459
01:07:16,223 --> 01:07:21,883
-Tomorrow?
-Tomorrow indeed. They'll attack then.

460
01:07:22,462 --> 01:07:26,022
-Osman Bey, I--
-Malhun Hatun.

461
01:07:27,878 --> 01:07:33,068
Tell me. Have you get used
to the tribe?

462
01:07:37,690 --> 01:07:41,690
-I will get used to it.
-What about...

463
01:07:41,690 --> 01:07:46,640
choosing women to help you?
-Alaca will be with me.

464
01:07:46,640 --> 01:07:51,300
And this Rum girl who lives in Söğüt,
Zoe.

465
01:07:51,300 --> 01:07:54,780
I talked to her. She'll be our helper,
if you allow it.

466
01:08:04,441 --> 01:08:07,361
Come here.

467
01:08:09,910 --> 01:08:13,320
Come, Malhun Hatun.

468
01:08:28,376 --> 01:08:32,816
-Tell me.
-Tell you what?

469
01:08:38,945 --> 01:08:42,305
What's your dream?

470
01:08:44,022 --> 01:08:48,682
What do you want in this
temporal world?

471
01:08:48,682 --> 01:08:53,252
What would you enjoy talking about?
Tell me.

472
01:08:54,811 --> 01:08:59,461
If you want to listen, let me tell you,
Osman Bey.

473
01:09:20,749 --> 01:09:25,899
It's the time we were waiting for, Nikola.
An army seeking Turkish blood awaits.

474
01:09:27,121 --> 01:09:31,121
No one can save Kayıs from us now.

475
01:09:32,950 --> 01:09:36,950
Turks say ''The arrow has already left
the bow''.

476
01:09:41,033 --> 01:09:46,163
We'll see who'll get shot.

477
01:09:59,348 --> 01:10:03,678
I told you I was going to make
Nicola my soldier.

478
01:10:04,256 --> 01:10:08,356
Nicola obeys me now.

479
01:10:08,893 --> 01:10:11,763
In the way of Genghis Khan...

480
01:10:12,123 --> 01:10:17,853
With the wrath of my father Noyan...

481
01:10:17,941 --> 01:10:21,851
Swords will spit blood..

482
01:10:22,761 --> 01:10:25,721
For Erlik Khan...

483
01:10:26,768 --> 01:10:29,658
- Death!
- Death! Death! Death!

484
01:10:33,804 --> 01:10:36,564
I am here for my father Noyan!

485
01:10:37,039 --> 01:10:40,389
Father, I am here for you!

486
01:10:40,935 --> 01:10:45,215
I am here to shed Turkish blood!

487
01:11:03,292 --> 01:11:06,872
To defeat Togay, we have to draw them
in a narrow valley, Aykurt.

488
01:11:07,066 --> 01:11:10,366
They are not used to fight somewhere
else than a moorland.

489
01:11:11,111 --> 01:11:14,881
We'll fight in a field, Turanalp.
Do not join if you don't want to.

490
01:11:16,610 --> 01:11:19,700
I have made my decision, Goktug.

491
01:11:44,244 --> 01:11:48,364
Alaca, you are a Kayı Hatun.

492
01:11:48,535 --> 01:11:50,085
Do not forget that.

493
01:11:50,287 --> 01:11:54,257
- You have to always listen to me.
- Don't worry, Aygül Hatun.

494
01:12:35,011 --> 01:12:40,051
Osman Bey, as you commanded, Umur Bey
will join us in Karacabey plateau.

495
01:12:40,074 --> 01:12:41,544
Eyvallah(okay) brother.

496
01:12:42,042 --> 01:12:43,322
Eyvallah.

497
01:12:59,311 --> 01:13:04,011
Bamsı Bey is not with us but
his swords are, aren't they?

498
01:13:04,808 --> 01:13:08,298
- Aren't they, Cerkutay?
- His son Cerkutay...

499
01:13:08,687 --> 01:13:12,007
is going to take revenge, my Bey.

500
01:13:13,253 --> 01:13:15,153
This is the day.

501
01:13:17,498 --> 01:13:19,608
This is the day.

502
01:13:33,538 --> 01:13:35,178
My Alps!

503
01:13:36,952 --> 01:13:41,462
We were raised by the stories
Bamsı Bey told us.

504
01:13:41,940 --> 01:13:45,030
However, they were not just stories...

505
01:13:46,123 --> 01:13:52,663
They shall show the way to
our valiants, our sons.

506
01:13:58,863 --> 01:14:03,733
We are enhanced by the honor of
Bamsı Bey and Abdurrahman Ghazi.

507
01:14:04,010 --> 01:14:09,300
If we do not take revenge for them...

508
01:14:09,691 --> 01:14:13,525
Then the stories they told us shall
be haram to us!

509
01:14:13,525 --> 01:14:15,615
Let them be!

510
01:14:16,250 --> 01:14:20,453
Then the horses we ride to war
shall not carry us!

511
01:14:20,453 --> 01:14:22,163
They shall not!

512
01:14:22,340 --> 01:14:25,290
This way ends in vengeance.

513
01:14:25,663 --> 01:14:31,083
If we return, this world shall be
a dungeon to us!

514
01:14:31,092 --> 01:14:32,942
It shall be!

515
01:14:35,328 --> 01:14:50,738
Allah-u Akbar!
(Allah is the greatest.

516
01:15:47,260 --> 01:15:50,110
This is the most difficult part of
being a Bey's Hatun.

517
01:15:53,207 --> 01:15:54,937
To wait.

518
01:15:59,922 --> 01:16:01,922
I am not used to this.

519
01:16:02,539 --> 01:16:05,429
I was always with my father.

520
01:16:05,495 --> 01:16:07,515
I was there in wars.

521
01:16:09,509 --> 01:16:12,409
This is how it's like to be
a tent Hatun.

522
01:16:13,186 --> 01:16:15,496
You just wait.

523
01:16:32,895 --> 01:16:35,025
You know what to do.

524
01:16:37,799 --> 01:16:42,429
Do not disobey me.

525
01:16:42,757 --> 01:16:45,382
This is your game, Togay.

526
01:16:45,692 --> 01:16:51,902
My soldiers will cover all the ways out.
We won't let any Turk run away.

527
01:16:53,853 --> 01:16:57,133
Yason, lead your soldiers.

528
01:17:05,919 --> 01:17:08,299
Osman's head is mine.

529
01:17:09,006 --> 01:17:15,076
No, Togay. Whoever wants more
will take it.

530
01:17:24,636 --> 01:17:27,236
Osman is coming

531
01:18:20,245 --> 01:18:22,485
They are waiting for us, my Bey.

532
01:18:22,956 --> 01:18:27,086
That's fine, our prey came to us.

533
01:18:35,879 --> 01:18:37,919
Soldier!

534
01:18:39,483 --> 01:18:41,083
Get ready!

535
01:18:42,898 --> 01:18:45,548
Soldiers! Get ready!

536
01:18:49,587 --> 01:18:52,307
Soldiers, get ready!

537
01:19:11,054 --> 01:19:12,763
Come to me.

538
01:19:12,763 --> 01:19:15,320
Why don't we attack, Osman Bey?

539
01:19:15,320 --> 01:19:18,640
Umur Bey, be patient.

540
01:19:20,093 --> 01:19:21,773
Be patient.

541
01:19:22,708 --> 01:19:24,518
Come to me.

542
01:19:26,628 --> 01:19:28,488
Attack!

543
01:19:30,625 --> 01:19:34,315
Geyhatu's hunter dog
Black Shaman Togay!

544
01:19:36,300 --> 01:19:38,720
We are even now!

545
01:19:46,669 --> 01:19:48,919
We are even!

546
01:19:53,971 --> 01:19:55,931
Just now.

547
01:21:01,129 --> 01:21:06,609
Seljuq Sultan says Togay is a rebel.

548
01:21:08,546 --> 01:21:14,446
Helping Togay meant recieving
Ilkhanate's support.

549
01:21:14,969 --> 01:21:17,219
But now, it means opposing Ilkhanate.

550
01:21:17,955 --> 01:21:22,805
Ilkhanate state on one side, Kayi tribe
on the other side.

551
01:21:23,982 --> 01:21:25,412
Nicola.

552
01:21:28,463 --> 01:21:30,593
Are you that strong?

553
01:21:31,765 --> 01:21:36,955
Or is Togay, who escapes from his
own state, strong enough?

554
01:21:42,359 --> 01:21:45,629
Only one reason is not enough, Gündüz Bey.

555
01:21:46,172 --> 01:21:48,782
You need more...

556
01:21:49,401 --> 01:21:52,031
If you want me to betray.

557
01:21:55,867 --> 01:22:01,617
Isn't it enough that we let you keep...

558
01:22:02,180 --> 01:22:04,050
your head on your body?

559
01:22:37,187 --> 01:22:38,887
Alps!

560
01:22:39,908 --> 01:22:42,138
For Bamsı Bey!

561
01:22:42,774 --> 01:22:47,724
For Abdurrahman Ghazi!
For all of our martyrs!

562
01:22:47,906 --> 01:22:50,056
Attack!

563
01:22:53,272 --> 01:22:55,632
In the name of Erlik Han...

564
01:22:56,704 --> 01:22:59,714
Slaughter them!

565
01:24:47,223 --> 01:24:49,353
Wait alps!

566
01:24:50,148 --> 01:24:52,158
Wait.

567
01:25:23,199 --> 01:25:25,159
Cowards!

568
01:25:53,242 --> 01:25:57,772
Togay, Togay, Togay.

569
01:25:59,006 --> 01:26:03,389
You knocked the door of
the angel of death...

570
01:26:03,389 --> 01:26:06,809
by disobeying the heir of Geyhatu..

571
01:26:06,870 --> 01:26:10,520
by disobeying me, disobeying Yargucu!

572
01:26:15,017 --> 01:26:16,967
Osman Bey!

573
01:26:27,857 --> 01:26:29,947
Vali Yargucu!

574
01:26:31,293 --> 01:26:37,183
This dog who violated the agreement and
killed my alps...

575
01:26:38,060 --> 01:26:40,010
is mine!

576
01:26:44,511 --> 01:26:46,601
Osman Bey!

577
01:26:46,834 --> 01:26:50,264
I'll take Togay to Sivas!

578
01:26:50,663 --> 01:26:54,883
I'll show everyone how the disobeyers
end up.

579
01:26:55,612 --> 01:26:58,732
Do not insist!

580
01:26:58,985 --> 01:27:01,795
Otherwisei you'll pay dearly.

581
01:27:39,780 --> 01:27:41,590
Bring them!

582
01:28:17,152 --> 01:28:19,472
Osman Bey, what are we going to do?

583
01:28:19,796 --> 01:28:22,496
Are we done with this ignoble dog here?

584
01:28:22,721 --> 01:28:25,201
Don't worry brother.

585
01:28:25,781 --> 01:28:29,001
It is not over...

586
01:28:30,415 --> 01:28:32,265
until Osman Bey says so.

587
01:28:40,163 --> 01:28:41,973
Alps!

588
01:28:42,504 --> 01:28:44,954
Alps! Clear the way!

589
01:29:03,728 --> 01:29:05,468
Hurry!

590
01:29:06,906 --> 01:29:08,646
Take them!

591
01:29:59,680 --> 01:30:04,340
I'll kill you in a
meeting of Noyans in Sivas.

592
01:30:04,983 --> 01:30:10,603
Everybody will see that disobeying
Geyhatu means disobeying me.

593
01:30:12,940 --> 01:30:16,950
Why did you obey this betrayer?

594
01:30:17,606 --> 01:30:22,886
You diverged from Genghis Khan's rules,
Yargucu! You sold your soul for gold!

595
01:30:22,964 --> 01:30:26,057
My soul is not for sale!

596
01:30:26,057 --> 01:30:28,067
Crush him!

597
01:31:50,014 --> 01:31:52,414
Stop!

598
01:31:53,428 --> 01:31:57,948
Stop!
Death is his salvation!

599
01:31:58,908 --> 01:32:01,708
He'll walk to Sivas.

600
01:32:01,918 --> 01:32:04,688
I'll crush him in each step of mine!

601
01:32:05,042 --> 01:32:10,032
He'll pay for treason in each step!

602
01:32:11,325 --> 01:32:13,095
We're leaving!

603
01:32:39,433 --> 01:32:42,783
My Bey, they took the way
near the Gorklu Mountain.

604
01:32:42,783 --> 01:32:45,183
There are too many places to set
an ambush.

605
01:32:46,162 --> 01:32:48,252
They were too many, Osman Bey.

606
01:32:48,654 --> 01:32:53,034
If we fight, we'll have so much martyrs.

607
01:32:56,445 --> 01:33:00,285
We'll handle, but not by fighting.

608
01:33:01,231 --> 01:33:06,501
We are going to have many opportunities
until they arrive in Sivas.

609
01:33:32,069 --> 01:33:34,319
You took revenge for my soldiers.

610
01:33:34,647 --> 01:33:37,537
ı appreciate you, High Nicola.

611
01:33:37,674 --> 01:33:40,984
I am raising my glass for you.

612
01:33:42,682 --> 01:33:45,892
To our victory and you.

613
01:33:47,306 --> 01:33:50,576
To our victory and you!

614
01:33:58,125 --> 01:34:02,355
Togay ended himself by
betraying his master.

615
01:34:02,964 --> 01:34:07,604
Nicola, the victory you won by
not facing Geyhatu...

616
01:34:07,908 --> 01:34:09,968
impowered us.

617
01:34:11,037 --> 01:34:14,497
What about Osman?
Not only us, Yason...

618
01:34:14,634 --> 01:34:19,464
Osman Bey gained strenght too.
Umur Bey and other Beys joined him.

619
01:34:19,641 --> 01:34:23,151
As I heard, he has
Seljuqi Sultan's support.

620
01:34:23,250 --> 01:34:26,650
Seljuqi Sultan needs to
cover himself first!

621
01:34:29,759 --> 01:34:35,039
If Sultan wants to face Byzantine Emperor
to protect Osman, I won't stop him.

622
01:34:35,762 --> 01:34:37,992
- To victory!
- To victory!

623
01:34:38,331 --> 01:34:41,081
So you used Nicola, huh?

624
01:34:46,347 --> 01:34:50,817
If we could have killed Togay,
we'd have a great victory.

625
01:34:52,975 --> 01:34:59,145
However, as Togay is still alive...

626
01:34:59,224 --> 01:35:02,114
he continues to be a threat for us,
Osman Bey.

627
01:35:07,809 --> 01:35:10,539
How did you convince Nicola, my Bey?

628
01:35:12,570 --> 01:35:17,650
When Vali learned Togay
disobeyed him...

629
01:35:19,239 --> 01:35:24,289
Sultan Mesud sent me a secret messenger.

630
01:35:26,992 --> 01:35:30,282
Politics paved the way for victory.

631
01:35:31,482 --> 01:35:35,952
Sultan showed that he valued
Osman Bey.

632
01:35:36,460 --> 01:35:40,870
So you used Nicola with this information.

633
01:35:42,264 --> 01:35:47,574
Vali may have ruined Osman Bey's plan...

634
01:35:49,027 --> 01:35:51,997
but we don't have a trouble like
Togay anymore.

635
01:35:55,004 --> 01:35:58,654
He can't escape from Vali Yargucu.

636
01:36:03,874 --> 01:36:08,694
My Bey, we know you won't stop.

637
01:36:09,456 --> 01:36:11,776
What is your plan?

638
01:36:17,274 --> 01:36:20,304
Bamsı Bey was my father's memorial.

639
01:36:21,117 --> 01:36:25,407
I considered him a father.
If I don't take revenge...

640
01:36:25,622 --> 01:36:28,552
The sky and the ground will
cast me out!

641
01:36:30,628 --> 01:36:34,008
I would upset my Beys!

642
01:36:35,110 --> 01:36:40,650
Brother, how can I sleep when
I go to bed?

643
01:36:51,955 --> 01:36:53,955
I have...

644
01:36:56,799 --> 01:36:58,949
a promise for Bamsı Bey.

645
01:37:00,729 --> 01:37:06,009
I am going to take revenge for him and
martyr Alps from Togay!

646
01:37:11,532 --> 01:37:16,332
I swear that Togay's death is going to be...

647
01:37:18,785 --> 01:37:21,185
committed by me!

648
01:37:22,879 --> 01:37:24,999
Inshallah (if Allah permits).

649
01:37:30,799 --> 01:37:32,149
Osman Bey.

650
01:37:33,357 --> 01:37:36,847
How are we going to take that dog
from Vail's hands?

651
01:37:41,405 --> 01:37:46,125
If we face Ilkhanate, all the
relationship you've been working on...

652
01:37:46,582 --> 01:37:49,012
will be ruined.

653
01:37:51,706 --> 01:37:54,896
This would surpass us.

654
01:38:01,372 --> 01:38:04,822
You are right, Umur Bey.
You are right.

655
01:38:04,851 --> 01:38:10,301
But I am not going to oppose Ilkhanate,
I'm going to oppose just Togay to kill him.

656
01:38:12,637 --> 01:38:16,107
I'll catch him while he runs away
from Vali.

657
01:38:18,763 --> 01:38:23,133
Brother!
Get the alps ready.

658
01:38:24,860 --> 01:38:27,860
We're going to do one last mission
for Bamsı Bey.

659
01:38:32,429 --> 01:38:38,609
Osman Bey, Vali will pass through
Germiyan land to arrive Sivas.

660
01:38:39,375 --> 01:38:42,505
He's going to spend the night there.

661
01:38:43,971 --> 01:38:48,411
I witnessed so many times that they
used that way.

662
01:38:49,444 --> 01:38:52,594
They are good with Germiyan Bey.

663
01:38:55,446 --> 01:38:57,826
Germiyan Land, huh?

664
01:39:05,202 --> 01:39:08,012
This information is handy.

665
01:39:13,269 --> 01:39:15,629
Who knows Germiyan land the best is...

666
01:39:18,417 --> 01:39:20,237
Turanalp.

667
01:39:27,295 --> 01:39:30,895
- Boran!
- My Bey.

668
01:39:31,959 --> 01:39:34,379
Summon Turanalp immediately!

669
01:39:34,986 --> 01:39:36,726
Yes my Bey.

670
01:40:02,675 --> 01:40:04,625
Can I come in?

671
01:40:07,144 --> 01:40:08,954
Come.

672
01:40:17,346 --> 01:40:21,226
They're searching for Togay everywhere.
They'll find Geyhatu's dog eventually.

673
01:40:21,917 --> 01:40:23,617
I know.

674
01:40:42,894 --> 01:40:47,384
A new bride shouldn't have
such mournful eyes, Malhun Hatun?

675
01:40:51,519 --> 01:40:54,989
The new bride is going to pale in this
tent like a wildflower, Alaca.

676
01:40:54,989 --> 01:40:59,636
You are not only a beautiful wildflower,
you are now a Hatun of Kayı tribe.

677
01:40:59,636 --> 01:41:01,436
Don't talk like that.

678
01:41:04,860 --> 01:41:11,270
I climed over the mountains with my sword,
fighting like a man.

679
01:41:11,421 --> 01:41:14,601
I am glad to have a fellow like you.

680
01:41:17,085 --> 01:41:19,985
I'll be your friend until the end,
Malhun Hatun.

681
01:41:20,063 --> 01:41:25,023
But, Osman Bey is the man
of your heart.

682
01:41:25,031 --> 01:41:30,011
He is the man of your tent.
Look where you are.

683
01:41:30,627 --> 01:41:32,677
Look around.

684
01:41:33,395 --> 01:41:37,625
You are in the tent of a man
who you fell in love with.

685
01:41:39,044 --> 01:41:44,214
I reached the happy end, is that right?

686
01:41:44,496 --> 01:41:48,076
Yes, thank Lord we've come this far.

687
01:41:48,294 --> 01:41:51,104
I am so happy for you.

688
01:41:52,590 --> 01:41:57,180
Do you think I don't realise
your love for Osman Bey in your eyes?

689
01:41:57,437 --> 01:42:01,267
Do you think I don't know
how much your heart wants him?

690
01:42:01,879 --> 01:42:04,959
Do you think Osman Bey doesn't know it?

691
01:42:09,247 --> 01:42:11,123
He knows, isn't he?

692
01:42:11,123 --> 01:42:12,693
Of course.

693
01:42:13,745 --> 01:42:18,705
If he knows, how are our hearts
going to meet...

694
01:42:19,595 --> 01:42:22,515
while our even our eyes can't meet?
Tell me Alaca.

695
01:42:27,981 --> 01:42:31,331
Bamsı Bey was like his father.

696
01:42:32,163 --> 01:42:35,363
He just lost his father.

697
01:42:36,738 --> 01:42:39,218
And now, it's Bamsı Bey.

698
01:42:46,162 --> 01:42:51,019
Isn't this what describes love,
Mahlun Hatun? To yearn for beloved one...

699
01:42:51,019 --> 01:42:53,619
and the sorrow of this.

700
01:42:56,780 --> 01:43:02,780
He doesn't share his sorrow, his pain,
even his happiness with me.

701
01:43:03,392 --> 01:43:05,782
How can he share his love with me?

702
01:43:05,972 --> 01:43:08,942
Our eyes can't even meet in
uncharted nights.

703
01:43:09,736 --> 01:43:12,376
My love can't reach him.

704
01:43:24,914 --> 01:43:26,444
Malhun.

705
01:43:28,709 --> 01:43:31,599
You should leave.
I have work to do.

706
01:44:01,034 --> 01:44:03,144
Oh Osman Bey.

707
01:44:05,845 --> 01:44:08,535
I wish you let me be with you.

708
01:44:09,858 --> 01:44:12,758
I wish you looked me in the eye.

709
01:44:44,433 --> 01:44:47,913
I wish you let me put my head
over your knee.

710
01:45:09,842 --> 01:45:13,642
Welcome sir. Welcome.
You brought us honor.

711
01:45:14,690 --> 01:45:18,133
I sent away everyone as I heard
you were coming.

712
01:45:18,133 --> 01:45:20,923
No one is here except for you.

713
01:45:21,724 --> 01:45:27,164
Sir, I made spare rib for you.
I know you love it.

714
01:45:27,246 --> 01:45:30,676
Hurry up.
I had a long way.

715
01:45:31,000 --> 01:45:34,390
My soldiers on guard outside
are also hungry!

716
01:45:34,907 --> 01:45:39,697
Set Vali Hadrat's table at once!
Carry food to thesoldiers!

717
01:45:59,042 --> 01:46:01,462
Take them to basement.

718
01:46:01,672 --> 01:46:03,432
Don't worry sir.

719
01:46:03,596 --> 01:46:08,886
There is a cell that even a mouse
can't enter.

720
01:46:09,304 --> 01:46:11,534
Take them, take them!

721
01:46:13,741 --> 01:46:15,021
Son.

722
01:46:17,637 --> 01:46:21,187
Show the way to soldiers.

723
01:47:35,224 --> 01:47:36,914
Tell me.

724
01:47:38,844 --> 01:47:43,134
There are tens of soldiers, my Bey.

725
01:47:43,688 --> 01:47:45,648
We can't get near.

726
01:47:48,913 --> 01:47:54,723
Keep your eyes wide open until Turanalp
brings Togay.

727
01:48:08,793 --> 01:48:11,533
How can my Bey trust him so much, Boran?

728
01:48:11,658 --> 01:48:13,608
He is a newbie.

729
01:49:33,948 --> 01:49:35,978
What are we going to do Togay?

730
01:49:37,924 --> 01:49:42,884
You sharpen your teeth if you don't
have a sword.

731
01:49:45,831 --> 01:49:50,441
Let your wrath keep you strong.

732
01:50:25,661 --> 01:50:27,571
I brought food.

733
01:50:54,058 --> 01:50:55,968
Clumsy idiot!

734
01:50:57,566 --> 01:51:00,092
I got it.

735
01:51:00,092 --> 01:51:02,222
Hurry up!

736
01:51:02,689 --> 01:51:05,049
What is this mess?

737
01:51:06,970 --> 01:51:10,260
Did you drop the food?
You clumsy!

738
01:51:15,381 --> 01:51:18,631
I can get you out of here
in return of a good deal of gold.

739
01:51:22,256 --> 01:51:23,766
How?

740
01:51:23,992 --> 01:51:26,652
Gold is a key to all the doors, Togay.

741
01:51:33,405 --> 01:51:35,965
I'll wait for you.

742
01:51:37,907 --> 01:51:39,827
Togay!
Leave the man!

743
01:51:43,823 --> 01:51:45,693
Get out of there.

744
01:52:26,909 --> 01:52:29,479
Can we trust this man, Togay?

745
01:52:33,610 --> 01:52:38,880
We won't trust him.
We'll trust the power of gold.

746
01:52:40,451 --> 01:52:42,241
If we go to Sivas...

747
01:52:44,286 --> 01:52:46,516
we're done.

748
01:53:28,879 --> 01:53:30,579
Stop there.

749
01:54:20,479 --> 01:54:22,319
Follow me.

750
01:54:27,355 --> 01:54:29,155
Come on!

751
01:54:34,131 --> 01:54:38,371
There are too many soldiers outside.
Where are we going to go?

752
01:54:38,784 --> 01:54:41,974
I know a secret passage.
Let's go.

753
01:54:58,804 --> 01:55:01,034
Togay, Togay.

754
01:55:01,897 --> 01:55:05,777
Turan will bring that dog safe
and sound, inshallah (if Allah permits).

755
01:55:06,014 --> 01:55:07,934
Inshallah.

756
01:55:09,590 --> 01:55:12,920
This is not a mission
for a new guy in the tribe.

757
01:55:18,269 --> 01:55:20,279
He is the guy, I think.

758
01:55:23,906 --> 01:55:29,046
Either he brings Togay, or
I know what to do.

759
01:58:19,535 --> 01:58:22,875
He'll get Togay among all those
animals...

760
01:58:23,255 --> 01:58:25,695
and convince him, then bring
him here.

761
01:58:28,300 --> 01:58:31,140
Turanalp's mission is extremely difficult,
Osman Bey.

762
01:58:31,415 --> 01:58:34,555
A valiant shines in such missions,
brother.

763
01:58:35,173 --> 01:58:37,950
He'll overcome for sure.

764
01:58:37,950 --> 01:58:39,620
Inshallah (If Allah permits)

765
01:58:47,136 --> 01:58:49,466
Come on, hurry up!

766
01:59:10,272 --> 01:59:12,512
Why did we stop?

767
02:00:03,798 --> 02:00:05,518
Togay!

768
02:00:42,712 --> 02:00:44,332
Osman.

769
02:00:58,102 --> 02:01:00,682
Pagan Noyan's son...

770
02:01:01,684 --> 02:01:04,064
Pagan Togay.

771
02:01:05,597 --> 02:01:08,327
Now wish luck from your Gods.

772
02:01:19,104 --> 02:01:22,024
I have been fighting for my father
for a long time.

773
02:01:23,149 --> 02:01:25,849
Let my teeth taste blood, Osman Bey.

774
02:01:26,381 --> 02:01:29,771
So you want to fight me, huh?

775
02:01:30,516 --> 02:01:33,576
Toe to toe.

776
02:01:35,211 --> 02:01:37,231
Toe to toe.

777
02:01:46,092 --> 02:01:48,252
Alps!

778
02:01:52,922 --> 02:01:54,682
Alps!

779
02:02:01,677 --> 02:02:07,177
For your holy soul, father!

780
02:02:54,460 --> 02:02:59,390
Gokboru, souls shall...

781
02:03:00,741 --> 02:03:02,621
take your life!

782
02:03:03,753 --> 02:03:09,023
From now on, our Lord shall help you.

783
02:03:09,504 --> 02:03:11,334
Go now.

784
02:08:03,870 --> 02:08:08,710
A wolf herd continues as a wolf herd.

785
02:08:10,615 --> 02:08:15,205
Your teeth can't bite Gokboru.

786
02:08:23,112 --> 02:08:28,792
Everyone will take a lesson
from your death.

787
02:08:31,602 --> 02:08:33,132
Now...

788
02:08:39,380 --> 02:08:41,570
it's time to take revenge!

789
02:08:41,933 --> 02:09:04,933
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com